{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[],"color":"#F39C12","description":"His loving parents. Arliden the bard and Laurian the noble-born.","name":"Arliden & Laurian"},{"children":[],"color":"#F39C12","description":"A life of music, acting, campfires, and endless fairs.","name":"Life on the Road"},{"children":[],"color":"#F39C12","description":"A close-knit family of performers. 'One Family'.","name":"The Troupe"}],"color":"#E67E22","description":"Kvothe's idyllic childhood with his family's troupe, the Edema Ruh, known as Lord Greyfallow's Men.","name":"The Edema Ruh"},{"children":[{"children":[],"color":"#5DADE2","description":"Kvothe witnesses Ben calling the name of the wind to stop a constable.","name":"Calling the Wind"},{"children":[],"color":"#5DADE2","description":"Lessons in Chemistry, Rhetoric, Arithmetic, and Logic.","name":"The Sciences"},{"children":[],"color":"#2980B9","description":"Learning the basics of magic: Alar and the Heart of Stone.","name":"Sympathy"},{"children":[],"color":"#2980B9","description":"Ben leaves the troupe at Hallowfell, warning them to 'Be wary of folly'.","name":"Departing Warning"}],"color":"#3498DB","description":"Meeting Ben, the old arcanist who joins the troupe and becomes Kvothe's first teacher.","name":"The Arcanist Abenthy"},{"children":[{"children":[],"color":"#AF7AC5","description":"Arliden pieces together old stories and fragments.","name":"Research"},{"children":[],"color":"#8E44AD","description":"Unknowingly speaking the true names of the Chandrian, drawing their attention.","name":"The Dangerous Name"}],"color":"#9B59B6","description":"Arliden's obsessive composition of a song about the tragic hero Lanre and the Chandrian.","name":"The Song of Lanre"},{"children":[{"children":[],"color":"#34495E","description":"Kvothe returns to find the camp destroyed, bodies found, and fires burning cold blue.","name":"The Blue Fire"},{"children":[],"color":"#34495E","description":"Signs of the Seven: Rusted iron wheels and instantly rotted wood.","name":"Iron and Rot"},{"children":[],"color":"#000000","description":"Confronting the white-haired Cinder and the shadow-cloaked Haliax.","name":"Cinder & Haliax"},{"children":[],"color":"#7F8C8D","description":"The Chandrian flee from 'The Amyr' or 'Singers', leaving Kvothe alive alone in the wreckage.","name":"The Escape"}],"color":"#2C3E50","description":"The tragic massacre of the troupe while Kvothe is away in the woods.","name":"The Chandrian Attack"}],"color":"#8B4513","name":"Kvothe: The Beginning"}